{"run_name": "toolcall_ab_t1_k5f_veerman_unsloth_Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF_UD-IQ3_XXS_20261109_163455", "suite": "veerman", "model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF:UD-IQ3_XXS", "model_slug": "unsloth_Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF_UD-IQ3_XXS", "case_id": "veerman_p9_code_trick", "category": "veerman_restraint", "split": "veerman", "prompt": "Can you write a Python script that checks the weather using an API?", "expected_tools": [], "multi_turn": false, "timestamp": "2026-11-09T16:35:18.398750", "turn_1_elapsed_s": 5.211, "turn_1_tool_calls": [], "turn_1_text": "Sure. Here’s a simple Python script that checks the current weather using the OpenWeatherMap API:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport requests\n\ndef get_weather(city: str, api_key: str = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fetch current weather for a city using the OpenWeatherMap API.\n    \"\"\"\n    if api_key is None:\n        api_key = os.getenv(\"OPENWEATHER_API_KEY\")\n\n    if not api_key:\n        raise ValueError(\"API key required. Set OPENWEATHER_API_KEY or pass api_key.\")\n\n    url = \"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather\"\n\n    params = {\n        \"q\": city,\n        \"appid\": api_key,\n        \"units\": \"metric\"  # Use \"imperial\" for Fahrenheit\n    }\n\n    response = requests.get(url, params=params)\n    response.raise_for_status()\n\n    return response.json()\n\n\ndef main():\n    city = input(\"Enter city name: \").strip()\n\n    try:\n        weather = get_weather(city)\n\n        name = weather[\"name\"]\n        temp = weather[\"main\"][\"temp\"]\n        feels_like = weather[\"main\"][\"feels_like\"]\n        humidity = weather[\"main\"][\"humidity\"]\n        description = weather[\"weather\"][0][\"description\"]\n\n        print(f\"Weather in {name}:\")\n        print(f\"Temperature: {temp:.1f}°C\")\n        print(f\"Feels like: {feels_like:.1f}°C\")\n        print(f\"Humidity: {humidity}%\")\n        print(f\"Conditions: {description.capitalize()}\")\n\n    except requests.HTTPError:\n        print(\"Error: Could not fetch weather data. Check the city name or API key.\")\n    except KeyError:\n        print(\"Error: Unexpected response from API.\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An error occurred: {e}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nInstall the dependency with:\n\n```bash\npip install requests\n```\n\nSet your API key using an environment variable:\n\n```bash\nexport OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=\"your_api_key_here\"\n```\n\nThen run:\n\n```bash\npython weather.py\n```", "turn_1_finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 613, "completion_tokens": 613, "total_tokens": 1226, "tok_s": 117.64, "engine_generation_tps": null, "engine_prompt_tps": null, "engine_peak_memory_gb": null, "turn_2_elapsed_s": null, "turn_2_tool_calls": null, "turn_2_text": null, "turn_2_usage": null, "reasoning_chars": 604, "score_pass": true, "score_reason": null, "score_breakdown": {"no_tool_correct": true, "clarified": null}, "temperature": 1.0, "top_p": 0.95, "reasoning_effort": "xhigh", "sampling_extra": {"top_k": 20, "min_p": 0.0, "presence_penalty": 0.0, "repetition_penalty": 1.0}, "seed": 42, "gpu_temp_c": null, "cpu_temp_c": null, "gpu_temp_after_c": null, "swap_used_mb": 1743, "swap_after_mb": 1743, "free_pages": 77342, "error": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "raw_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "Sure. Here’s a simple Python script that checks the current weather using the OpenWeatherMap API:\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport requests\n\ndef get_weather(city: str, api_key: str = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Fetch current weather for a city using the OpenWeatherMap API.\n    \"\"\"\n    if api_key is None:\n        api_key = os.getenv(\"OPENWEATHER_API_KEY\")\n\n    if not api_key:\n        raise ValueError(\"API key required. Set OPENWEATHER_API_KEY or pass api_key.\")\n\n    url = \"https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather\"\n\n    params = {\n        \"q\": city,\n        \"appid\": api_key,\n        \"uni